    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance measurements. It assumes a system where a single logical model is served across multiple nodes/GPUs, or where multiple replicas serve behind a coordinator.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal: Prove that every node is running the exact same logical system.**\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash**: Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must match. Verify the hash *after* loading, not just from the manifest \u2014 catch cases where a node silently falls back to a cached or local copy.\n- [ ] **Tokenizer identity**: Confirm tokenizer version, vocabulary size, special-token map, and chat template are identical across nodes. A mismatched chat template can pass smoke tests but corrupt multi-turn behavior.\n- [ ] **Code and build identity**: Record git commit, Docker image digest (not just tag), and build flags per node. Tags are mutable; digests are not.\n- [ ] **Parallelism configuration**: Document tensor-parallel (TP), pipeline-parallel (PP), expert-parallel (EP), and data-parallel (DP) degrees. Confirm the product of TP\u00d7PP\u00d7EP matches the number of GPUs allocated per replica, and DP\u00d7(TP\u00d7PP\u00d7EP) matches total GPUs.\n- [ ] **Quantization/dtype consistency**: Verify weight dtype, KV-cache dtype, and activation dtype are as configured on every shard. A single node running FP16 KV cache while others run FP8 will produce subtle quality drift and inconsistent memory headroom.\n- [ ] **Sampling parameter defaults**: Confirm identical default temperature, top-p, top-k, seed handling, and max-context settings across replicas.",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
